# UI primitives from the kit, mobile first

## Pyramid Layer

- Layer: leaf (presentation).

## Use This When

- A view needs a button, input, card, menu, select, dialog or any other control.

## Stop Here If

- Every control comes from `@workspace/ui` and the layout works at 360 CSS px wide.

## Descend To

- Vendor skill: `.agents/skills/shadcn/SKILL.md` (this project uses the Base UI line).

## Core rule

- No raw `<button>`, `<input>` or `<select>` in views; use the `@workspace/ui` primitives. Raw elements are fine for layout only.
- A class cluster that repeats becomes a `cva` variant of the primitive, not a copy.
- One `Hint` wrapper for tooltips; the accessible name (`aria-label`) uses the same i18n key as the visible hint.
- Mobile first: unprefixed utilities describe the 360x640 layout; widen with `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`. No `max-*` variants without a comment that says why.
- Touch targets are at least 44x44 CSS px with 8 px between them; inputs use at least 16 px text.
- No horizontal scroll on any screen; e2e checks it after every step.
- `@workspace/ui` holds no copy and no domain knowledge: text and data arrive through props.
